<title>FRANCE: BoF declines comment on German gold move.</title>
<headline>BoF declines comment on German gold move.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France has no comment on reports Germany was planning to revalue its central bank gold reserves to reflect market prices, an official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Bank of France revalues its gold every six months to reflect market prices and is therefore not in the same situation as Germany, where Bundesbank gold reserves have not been revalued to reflect market rates.</p>
</text>
